[Audio:click:Click]
Played by #R$71D3. One click: the speaker is on for the time in #REGb and off
for the time in #REGd. This example uses #N$30 and #N$50. The noises are made
from clicks like this one.

#AUDIO0(click.wav)(#INCLUDE(Click))

[Audio:beep:Beep]
Played by #R$71E0. One cycle of a square wave, used as a beep by the sweeps
and the warbles. This example has a half-period of #N$60.

#AUDIO0(beep.wav)(#INCLUDE(Beep))

[Audio:arrival-sound:Arrival Sound]
Played by #R$71F0 at the end of the scroll when a life starts.
Thirty-two beeps, rising from a half-period of #N$90 down to #N$71.

#AUDIO0(arrival-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(ArrivalSound))

[Audio:pick-up-sound:Pick-Up Sound]
Played by #R$71FE when the ship picks up an object.
Sixteen beeps, rising from a half-period of #N$50 down to #N$41.

#AUDIO0(pick-up-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(PickUpSound))

[Audio:unused-sound:Unused Sound]
Played by #R$7204, which nothing calls.
Twenty-three clicks.

#AUDIO0(unused-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(UnusedSound))

[Audio:object-warble:Object Warble]
Played by #R$720A while an object is live and the ship is not exploding.
The pitch comes from the age of the object. This example is age #N($06),
which becomes stage #N$03 of the warble at #R$7217.

#AUDIO0(object-warble.wav)(#INCLUDE(ObjectWarble))

[Audio:warble:Warble]
Played by #R$7217. Four beeps that alternate between two notes.
This example is stage #N$02. Stages #N($07) and #N($08), and any stage of
#N$10 or more, are silent.

#AUDIO0(warble.wav)(#INCLUDE(Warble))

[Audio:flutter-sound:Flutter Sound]
Played by #R$7234. A flutter whose length comes from the low three bits of
the frame counter. This example is frame #N$03.

#AUDIO0(flutter-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(FlutterSound))

[Audio:hit-sound:Hit Sound]
Played by #R$724C when an object is hit, destroyed or damaged.
Sixteen beeps, falling.

#AUDIO0(hit-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(HitSound))

[Audio:change-sound:Change Sound]
Played by #R$725C when the colour of the ship changes.
Ten beeps, rising.

#AUDIO0(change-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(ChangeSound))

[Audio:bump-sound:Bump Sound]
Played by #R$7263 when an object hits the terrain.
Fifteen beeps, alternating between a very low note and a high note.

#AUDIO0(bump-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(BumpSound))

[Audio:moving-sound:Moving Sound]
Played by #R$7275 while an object moves, on odd frames. If bit 6 of offset
#N$16 is clear it is this short rising sweep of four beeps. Otherwise a
different sweep is played, once every four frames.

#AUDIO0(moving-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(MovingSound))

[Audio:crash-sound:Crash Sound]
Played by #R$7293 when the ship hits the terrain.
Twenty-eight clicks.

#AUDIO0(crash-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(CrashSound))

[Audio:short-crash-sound:Short Crash Sound]
Played by #R$72A5.
Eight clicks, with a different pattern from the crash.

#AUDIO0(short-crash-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(ShortCrashSound))

[Audio:explosion-sound:Explosion Sound]
Played by #R$72AB on each step of the explosion until the counter reaches
#N$2D. This example is step #N$0B: a warble, then a few clicks. Every eighth
step plays the falling note at #R$72CA instead, and the even steps after the
first are silent.

#AUDIO0(explosion-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(ExplosionSound))

[Audio:explosion-hit-sound:Explosion Hit Sound]
Played by #R$72CA on every eighth step of the explosion.
Seven beeps, falling.

#AUDIO0(explosion-hit-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(ExplosionHitSound))

[Audio:beam-sound:Beam Sound]
Played by #R$72CF for a beam. The clicks depend on the first three bytes of
the beam. This example uses #N($05), #N($03) and #N$10.

#AUDIO0(beam-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(BeamSound))

[Audio:shot-sound:Shot Sound]
Played by #R$72F2 when a shot starts. This example is the noise for an object
whose bit 7 of offset #N$16 is clear. The other bit plays a different noise.

#AUDIO0(shot-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(ShotSound))

[Audio:patterned-noise:Patterned Noise]
Played by #R$7303. The number of clicks and the pattern come from a value
from #N$00 to #N$03. This example is #N$01.

#AUDIO0(patterned-noise.wav)(#INCLUDE(PatternedNoise))

[Audio:noise-burst:Noise Burst]
Played by #R$7311.
Ten clicks.

#AUDIO0(noise-burst.wav)(#INCLUDE(NoiseBurst))

[Audio:removal-sound:Removal Sound]
Played by #R$7318 when an object is removed.
Ten beeps, rising.

#AUDIO0(removal-sound.wav)(#INCLUDE(RemovalSound))

[Audio:title-tune:Title Tune]
Played by #R$F26C from the notes at #R$70D8 while the title screen waits for
a key. Two hundred and fifty notes.

#AUDIO0(title-tune.wav)(#INCLUDE(TitleTune))

[Audio:game-start-tune:Game Start Tune]
Played by #R$F26C from the notes at #R$F4E4 after the menu has finished, just
before the game starts. Nine notes.

#AUDIO0(game-start-tune.wav)(#INCLUDE(GameStartTune))

[Audio:ship-destroyed-tune:Ship Destroyed Tune]
Played by #R$F48B from the notes at #R$F4DD once the explosion of the ship
has finished. Six notes.

#AUDIO0(ship-destroyed-tune.wav)(#INCLUDE(ShipDestroyedTune))

[Audio:planet-complete-tune:Planet Complete Tune]
Played by #R$F52A from the notes at #R$F56A when a planet has been completed.
Twenty-one notes.

#AUDIO0(planet-complete-tune.wav)(#INCLUDE(PlanetCompleteTune))

[Audio:game-over-tune:Game Over Tune]
Played by #R$F4FC from the notes at #R$F580 when the game is over.
Sixteen notes.

#AUDIO0(game-over-tune.wav)(#INCLUDE(GameOverTune))
